          <li><b>01 / NOW</b><span>AI is a powerful assistant for boilerplate, prototypes, and quick explanations—not a substitute for understanding the system.</span></li>
          <li><b>02 / NEXT</b><span>Engineers will steer agents and integrations by defining requirements, architecture, constraints, and failure cases.</span></li>
          <li><b>03 / ALWAYS</b><span>Verification, security, accessibility, human empathy, and a skeptical read of the diff stay stubbornly human responsibilities.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="wrap">
    <span><strong>The Human in the Loop</strong> · Built with curiosity and reviewed with care.</span>
    <span>Five humans. Zero unreviewed commits (in theory).</span>
  </footer>

<script>
  (() => {
    const button = document.querySelector(".theme-toggle");
    const label = document.querySelector(".theme-label");
    const icon = document.querySelector(".theme-icon");

    button.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const isNight = document.body.dataset.theme === "night";
      document.body.dataset.theme = isNight ? "day" : "night";
      button.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(!isNight));
      button.setAttribute("aria-label", isNight ? "Switch to night mode" : "Switch to day mode");
      label.textContent = isNight ? "Night mode" : "Day mode";
      icon.textContent = isNight ? "☾" : "☀";
    });
  })();
</script>
</body>
</html>
